<zk>
<!-- The invalid rows of the gallery pages set errorMessage, so ZK itself marks the field invalid and opens an
     errorbox. The rows show the field, not the box, so those fields set errorboxSclass="demo-errorbox-hidden" and
     this rule hides their errorboxes. The errorbox is a popup appended to the body, outside the field, so only the
     class ZK copies onto it reaches the right boxes; pages that demonstrate the errorbox (errorbox.zul) do not set
     it. Closing the boxes from script instead was tried: ZK creates the errorbox after mount at a time that
     varies with the first page load, so the box showed on a cold start. !important: the popup shows itself with an
     inline display. -->
<style>.demo-errorbox-hidden { display: none !important; }</style>
</zk>
